From af55cc0f78801261fc8c2707a500eca4b792276f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 21:44:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Error handling: MGIS_NOEXCEPT for the functions of the
 prototype reporting errors in a context

Since c1ee292 (#283), the functions which may report an error in a
context are declared MGIS_NOEXCEPT, which is empty if errors are reported
by exceptions (enable-exceptions), so that the exception reaches the
caller instead of terminating the process. The default build is
unchanged.

The functions of the prototype reporting errors in a context were still
noexcept: updateValues and updateInputValues taking field operations,
the setters and updateValues of the material state views, and the
internal functions they use (copies of the field holders, HDF5 files
written and read point by point). updateValues without operations, save
and restore, which are MGIS_NOEXCEPT, call them: with enable-exceptions,
their errors terminated the process.
---
 include/MGIS/Behaviour/MaterialDataView.hxx   |  8 ++---
 .../MGIS/Behaviour/MaterialStateManager.hxx   |  5 +--
 src/MaterialDataView.cxx                      | 10 +++---
 src/MaterialStateManager.cxx                  | 33 ++++++++++---------
 4 files changed, 30 insertions(+), 26 deletions(-)

